  "note": "Annual election of one third of the council (five seats) due on Wednesday 15 January 1902. Nine were nominated on Monday 6 January (Alexander Foster, Robert Hazelton, Thomas Hopps, Edward Lunn, James Millar Moore, Murtagh McCann, James McNeice, Thomas Ross, Robert Thompson), but five withdrew, leaving four for five seats, and there was no poll (\"for the first time in very many years\"). On Wednesday 8 January the returning officer, F. W. Pollock, declared Hazelton, Dr Moore, Lunn and Thompson elected, and also John McNally, J.P., a retiring member who had declined nomination: the law required the retiring member who had polled highest at his previous election to fill the vacant seat for another three years. Folder dated the statutory polling day. No party labels printed."
